                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p style="line-height: 2;"><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">This course is a professional compulsory course designed for undergraduate students majoring in pharmacy. Building on the solution equilibrium theory learned in the first year, students are expected to master the fundamental principles of four titrimetric analysis methods. They will also gain a comprehensive understanding of the experimental conditions and precautions for various chemical analysis methods, grasp the concept of error, and develop the ability to accurately process experimental data. Additionally, students will be equipped with knowledge of the application scopes of different analytical methods. This course lays a solid foundation for the study of “Pharmaceutical Analysis,” a core course for pharmacy majors in their junior year.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
